<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 56 — Autoscaling.
    hpa/        ReplicaCalculator (the HPA's replica count for a CPU utilization target, with unready and missing pods
                handled as Kubernetes 1.37 does) and ScalingBehavior (stabilization windows and rate policies)
    resources/  k8s/ (a Deployment sized for the HPA, and an autoscaling/v2 HPA with its behavior written out)
  verify/run.sh runs a real HPA on metrics-server (k3s 1.37) against menu-service under load: a load step up and
  down, pods whose startup CPU is or isn't counted, and load that comes and goes with and without a scale-down window.
-->
